const e="driven-talent-competition",d=2026,o="Built from the organiser's 2026 Official Rules & Regulations PDF (the 2025 edition has the same structure). No venue, dates, contacts or addresses are printed, so there are no such variables; fee amounts for registration are not printed, only the payment levels. The rules print the medal bands out of 300 for each level; the platform keeps one grade table, so bands are written here. Single-age divisions for Jazz, Tap, Lyrical, Contemporary and Open are not carried in the template.",n=JSON.parse(`{"Title":"Rules & Criteria","Subtitle":"Driven Talent Competition 2026 regional events and National Championships. Studios must follow these rules.","NoticeTitle":"Please Read Before Registering","Notice":"Ages are calculated on {{AgeCutoffDate}}. All entries are made online and all fees must be paid before the event. No refunds are given.","Notes":["Entries are first come, first served. No routines are added at the door.","Check the summary e-mail after payment and reply at once with any correction to a birth date or age division.","Level names in group names: Boundaries is Breaking Boundaries, Accel Stars is Accelerating Stars."],"Sections":[{"Key":"general","Title":"General Rules","Items":["Studios must follow all Rules and Regulations. Failure to comply may result in disqualification.","A routine name may not be exactly the same as the name of the studio.","The organiser may add competition days or change venues if necessary.","Rules are evaluated and enforced case by case, based on what is best for everyone involved.","The event is open to the general public.","The routine size classes are: Solo (1 performer), Duet/Trio (2 or 3), Small Group (4 to 9), Large Group (10 to 19), Line (20 or more) and Production Line (20 or more).","A group must perform with the number of performers it registered. If a performer is added or missing, the routine may be moved to the right group size. If that size has already performed, the routine is judged for adjudication only.","Performers added to a group that were not in the first registration must be added and paid for. The average age is calculated again.","Each routine is judged by a panel of judges. Judges' decisions are final.","The organiser's judges may move a routine to a higher level if they feel it was placed below its ability. If the new level has already competed, the routine is eligible for adjudication only.","If 1st place overall has a large point gap over the rest of the Top 10, that routine may be moved to the next highest level.","Acro and gymnastics tricks are limited to 3 per routine in dance categories. Open, Acro/Gymnastics and Production Line have no limit. Cheerleading may contain up to 50 percent acro/gymnastics.","A trick is a move where the feet leave the floor and the body inverts over the head while the hands have left the floor, except aerials (for example roundoffs, handsprings, tucks, pikes, layouts, fulls). A tumbling pass of several tricks counts as 1 trick. Lifts with several performers are not tricks.","At National Championships all rules, ages, levels, genres and group sizes from the regional events stay the same."]},{"Key":"eligibility","Title":"Eligibility","Items":["Every performer must be assigned one level when registered. A performer may be entered in one level only.","A performer's level is not changed once entered for the season. No levels are changed after the schedule is released or at the event.","Entries must give the accurate name and date of birth of every contestant.","Age is the performer's age on {{AgeCutoffDate}}. The age divisions are 5 and under, 6 to 8, 9 to 11, 12 to 14, 15 to 19 and 20 and over.","Duets, trios, groups and lines compete at the average age of all their dancers. Decimals are dropped (an average of 12.7 competes as age 12).","Any routine with a performer over age 19 competes in the Adult division. Adult routines are not eligible for Driven Dollars.","No performer may perform more than 1 age division lower than their own age. For example, a Senior (15 to 19) may not perform in a Junior (9 to 11) routine, whatever the average age. Production Lines are the exception.","A performer who competes with several studios must give written permission from each studio.","A performer attending an event with a studio may not compete as an Independent at that event. Independent entries are accepted only if the city has space.","Breaking Boundaries (Special Ability level) is for performers with different abilities who may face physical or developmental challenges. Scoring focuses on showmanship, memorization and musicality.","Starting Line (Beginner) is for pre-competitive performers with little or no competing experience who have danced no more than 2 years. A performer may stay in this level for a maximum of 2 years.","Accelerating Stars (Intermediate) is recommended for performers with about 2 to 5 years of competition experience.","Grand Prix (Advanced) is for competitive performers at an advanced technical level. Level choice uses years of competing as a first guide, then overall skill and weekly studio hours.","A Grand Prix performer may not perform in any Starting Line routine.","Level of a Duet/Trio or Small Group is the highest level of any performer in it. One Grand Prix performer and 8 Accelerating Stars performers make a Grand Prix routine.","In a Large Group or Line, no more than one third of the performers may be in a higher level than the routine's level. In a group of 15, 5 may be Grand Prix. In a group of 14, only 4 (the decimal is dropped).","Production Lines are always placed in the Grand Prix level. All Vocals default to the Grand Prix level.","Pointe is open to Grand Prix and Accelerating Stars levels only.","Grand Prix performers may enter a total of 4 Accelerating Stars Large Groups or Lines.","Title competition: the performer must be registered in Accelerating Stars or Grand Prix level."]},{"Key":"registration","Title":"How to Register","Items":["All reservations need a deposit to hold space. A reservation with no deposit may be removed within 2 weeks or sooner. Ask the registration office about exceptions.","All entries must be made online. No other format is accepted. Include all routines, because none are added at the door.","Entries are accepted first come, first served.","Registrations must be checked and finalized no less than 40 days before the event.","Changes made less than 21 days before the event cost {{ChangeFee}}. All changes must be in writing and the card on file is charged. If there is no card on file, one must be given first.","No level changes are made once the program has gone to print.","Music is uploaded through the registration system at least 5 days before the competition.","For the Title competition, tick the box when registering the solo online. Registration at the door is allowed at least 1 hour before the performance.","For the Costume Award, tick the box when registering the routine online, or enter at least half an hour before the performance.","The Driven Cypher improv at National Championships is registered at the Registration Desk. Space is limited.","The number of solos may be limited if a city has no time for more."]},{"Key":"fees","Title":"Fees and Payment","Items":["All fees must be paid in full to get the leveled prices: {{PaymentLevel1}} (level 1); {{PaymentLevel2}} (level 2); {{PaymentLevel3}} (level 3).","Payment is by debit or credit card (no card fee is added) or by direct ACH payment. ACH is not accepted later than 45 days before the event.","Certified checks, personal checks and money orders are not accepted.","All payments must be made no later than 30 days before the first day of the event. Late fees apply from 29 days before the event.","After payment the studio receives an e-mail summary of all routines. The studio must check it, including birth dates and age divisions, and reply at once with corrections.","All balances must be paid before the competition. No payments are accepted at the event. Entries must be paid in full before routines are scheduled.","No refunds are given for any reason.","Late changes: {{ChangeFee}}.","Extended time for Small Groups, Large Groups and Lines: {{ExtendedTimeFee}}. Lines are limited to a maximum of 6 minutes.","Props that need more than 2 minutes pay for extended time: {{PropTimeFee}}.","Costume contest: {{CostumeContestFee}}.","Driven Cypher improv entry at Nationals: {{CypherFee}}."]},{"Key":"teams","Title":"Entry Limits and Group Sizes","Items":["Solo: 1 performer. Duet/Trio: 2 or 3 performers. Small Group: 4 to 9. Large Group: 10 to 19. Line: 20 or more. Production Line: 20 or more.","A soloist may not compete against themselves in the same performance category.","Starting Line and Breaking Boundaries soloists may enter at most 2 solos. Other soloists may enter at most 3 solo performance categories. Vocal solos are not counted.","Starting Line performers may enter a total of 6 routines in the solo, duet/trio, small group and large group divisions together. There is no limit on lines or productions.","A Duet/Trio may not compete in the same performance category with exactly the same performers. At least 1 performer must be different to compete in the same age group and category.","A performer may enter the Title competition with at most 3 solos."]},{"Key":"levels","Title":"Levels, National Championships and Showdown","Items":["At every regional event a Title competition is part of the solo division.","National Championships feature the Rise of Legends Showdown. There is one version for Accelerating Stars and Starting Line performers and another for Grand Prix performers, on two separate days.","For the Showdown, the top 5 studio scores in Grand Prix and Accelerating Stars in the Small Group, Large Group and Line divisions in each overall age category (5 and under, 6 to 8, 9 to 11, 12 to 14, 15 to 19) are invited to recompete.","In the 11 and Under and 12 and Over Production Line divisions the top 5 studio scores also recompete in the Grand Prix Showdown.","In Starting Line, the top 5 studio scores in the combined 11 and Under and 12 and Over categories, whatever the group size, are invited to recompete.","Once a routine has qualified, performers, level, age division and group size cannot change. Changes are allowed only for illness or injury and only if level and age division stay the same.","Extra routines may be added if scores are tied or very close, as long as they are within the top ten.","In National Championships, Accelerating Stars titles are awarded the same way as at regionals.","Grand Prix only: the Race for the Crown Throwdown. During the week the top 3 to 5 Mr. and Miss finalists in each overall age category are announced. The same contestant may not place more than once. Finalists recompete in the Grand Prix Showdown for the title of Mr. and Miss Driven.","A National title winner may not compete for the same title in the same overall division and age category at the next season's Nationals, unless the performer moves to a new age category."]},{"Key":"judging","Title":"Judging and Scoring","Items":["Routines are measured against a set point scale and awarded by a medal system. Legendary is the highest in the Grand Prix level. Platinum is the highest in Accelerating Stars, Starting Line and Breaking Boundaries.","Grand Prix bands: Legendary 295 to 300; Platinum 290 to 294.9; Elite Gold 285 to 289.9; Gold 280 to 284.9; Elite Silver 275 to 279.9; Silver 270 to 274.9; Bronze 265 to 269.9.","Accelerating Stars bands: Legendary not eligible; Platinum 285 to 300; Elite Gold 280 to 284.9; Gold 275 to 279.9; Elite Silver 270 to 274.9; Silver 265 to 269.9; Bronze 260 to 264.9.","Starting Line bands: Legendary not eligible; Platinum 280 to 300; Elite Gold 275 to 279.9; Gold 270 to 274.9; Elite Silver 265 to 269.9; Silver 260 to 264.9; Bronze 255 to 259.9.","Breaking Boundaries bands: Legendary not eligible; Platinum 280 to 300; Elite Gold 275 to 279.9; Gold 270 to 274.9; Elite Silver 265 to 269.9; Silver 260 to 264.9; Bronze 255 to 259.9.","Routines over the time limit may lose points.","Music with profanity, racial slurs or other inappropriate lyrics gets an automatic point deduction.","A solo routine that is not completed the first time and is tried again may lose points.","A studio that delays the show because it is rehearsing backstage loses points from its total score.","Items left on stage may lead to removal from overall high scores. Liquids, paints, powders, chalk and glitter that reach the Marley floor and are not cleaned up may lead to disqualification or removal from overall high scores.","The Title competition is judged on showmanship, style and overall presentation. A competitor can receive a maximum of 10 points from each judge. All Title entries are judged during the performance of their solo.","Level placement cannot be protested because it is an opinion."]},{"Key":"points","Title":"High Score Awards and Points","Items":["If a category has 2 or more routines, the routine with the highest score gets a first place award. Each Solo and Duet/Trio winner receives an award.","Grand Prix: all solos, duets/trios, small groups, large groups, lines and production lines in each age division are eligible for High Score Awards. Grand Prix is the only level eligible for Driven Dollars and for the Highest Level Adjudication.","Starting Line, Accelerating Stars and Breaking Boundaries: all routines in each age division and level are eligible for High Score Awards. Special awards go to the highest score.","High Score age divisions are Mini (5 and under), Petite (6 to 8), Junior (9 to 11), Teen (12 to 14), Senior (15 to 19) and Adult (20 and over).","Solo: High Score Awards for the Top 10 soloists in each age division. A contestant may not place more than once. The organiser may announce more finalists.","Duet/Trio: High Score Awards for the Top 10 in each age division. The same duet/trio may not place more than once, and there must be a 50 percent difference in performers to be in the same age group of the same category.","Small Groups, Large Groups, Lines and Production Lines: High Score Awards for the Top 10 in each age division. The organiser may announce more finalists.","Driven's Studio Vanguard Award (Grand Prix Showdown): 1st place is 3 points, 2nd is 2 points, 3rd is 1 point. The studio with the most points wins."]},{"Key":"prizes","Title":"Awards and Prizes","Items":["Grand Prix first place overall gets Driven Dollars by routine size and number of entries at the event. Solo: {{DrivenDollarsSolo}}.","Duet/Trio: {{DrivenDollarsDuetTrio}}.","Small and Large Groups: {{DrivenDollarsGroup}}.","Lines and Production Lines: {{DrivenDollarsLine}}.","Industry Icon Award: 2 per show, given to the highest scoring group in the 11 and under and 12 and over combined divisions. Driven Dollars: {{IndustryIconDollars}}.","Driven Performance of the Week: the highest group score of each regional is announced on Instagram every Wednesday. A social media vote chooses the Driven Performance of the Year, and the winning studio gets a special gift.","Choreography Award: in both 11 and Under and 12 and Over, to the choreographer or studio of select groups, lines or productions.","Entertainment Award: in both 11 and Under and 12 and Over, to select groups, lines or productions.","The Right Track Award: in both 11 and Under and 12 and Over, to the studio with great sportsmanship, spirit and attitude.","Tap and Hip Hop Excellence Awards: in both 11 and Under and 12 and Over, to the most outstanding Tap and Hip Hop group routines.","Driven Dancers of the Week: one soloist chosen by the judges at each regional, announced on social media. At the end of the season the judging panels choose 5 finalists, a social media vote picks the Driven Dancer of the Year, who is featured in the 2026 Program and gets extra prizes.","Photogenic Award: to the Top 3 scores in the 11 and under and 12 and over divisions. A contestant may place once in the Top 3. Photos are returned after the awards ceremony and are not mailed.","Costume Award: to the Top 3 scores in each of 4 divisions: Solos (11 and under; 12 and over) and Group Costume with Duet/Trio, Groups and Lines combined (11 and under; 12 and over). Judged on originality, design and overall impression, during the routine. Enter at least half an hour before the performance.","Outstanding Vocalist Award: to the vocalist with the highest score in the 11 and under and the 12 and over divisions.","Title Awards: Mini Miss Driven and Mini Mr. Driven (5 and under); Petite Miss Driven and Little Mr. Driven (6 to 8); Junior Miss Driven and Junior Mr. Driven (9 to 11); Teen Miss Driven and Teen Mr. Driven (12 to 14); Miss Driven and Mr. Driven (15 to 19). Awards go to the male and female Title Champions and the 1st and 2nd runners-up in each age division. A contestant may not place more than once. Title entrants stay eligible for High Score Awards.","A regional Title Champion may not compete the same routine for Title at another regional event, but may compete a different routine at another regional that year.","Spirit Award (Nationals): a designated Spirit Day with a set theme. The winner is announced at the Grand Prix Showdown and receives Driven Dollars.","Driven's Studio Vanguard Award: the winning studio gets Driven Dollars, a banner and a featured studio photo in the next year's regional program.","National finalist awards, trophies and banners are given by placement in each age division and group size.","Industry Icon at the Grand Prix Showdown: winners in the Small Group, Large Group and Line divisions in each age category are considered. The 11 and Under and 12 and Over Production Lines are judged as separate categories.","In the Accelerating Stars and Starting Line Showdowns, the top scoring Accelerating Stars groups in the combined 11 and Under and 12 and Over categories decide the Industry Icon winners.","National title winners (Mr. and Miss Driven) get a trophy, sash and crown. The 1st and 2nd runners-up get a trophy."]},{"Key":"conduct","Title":"Music, Props and Conduct","Items":["Music is uploaded through the registration system at least 5 days before the competition.","If a file cannot be uploaded, bring a flash drive labeled with the studio name. Label each routine with its entry number and name, for example \\"452 - Yeah\\". Bring a backup of all music.","Props on stage have a maximum of 2 minutes to build and remove. Longer needs extended time: {{PropTimeFee}}.","Props may not be stored in the wings during the show. Props should be loaded in and out of the venue on the same day they are used.","All props must be fire-proofed. Tell the backstage manager about props before the performance.","No dangerous props such as fire, swords or knives, and no live animals, are allowed on stage.","Liquids, paints, powders, chalk and glitter may not touch the Marley floor. Anything transferred must be cleaned up at once by the studio.","Anything left on stage (props, petals, paper, leaves) must be cleaned up quickly by the studio.","No performer may kneel, stand or lie above 8 feet from the stage floor.","No special stage or house lighting is provided or changed for any performance.","Pre-check in backstage at least 1 hour before the first performance. Teachers may stay backstage for an appropriate time to prepare and watch. Backstage must be clear and organized at all other times.","No food, drinks or smoking in the performance area or inside the contracted venue. No alcohol or tobacco at events on school property. Smoking is not allowed in any venue.","Sportsmanlike behavior is expected from performers, studio owners, teachers and spectators. Failure to show it may lead to immediate disqualification and removal from the venue.","Video and photography in the competition auditorium are strictly prohibited and may lead to disqualification. The organiser may take the tape or delete the footage.","Contestants allow the organiser to use their photographs and videos, and to appear on local or national television, to promote its competitions.","The organiser and the host facility are not responsible for personal injury or property loss. Participation accepts the inherent risks of physical activity. Studio owners agree to the Release of Liability Clause completed during registration."]},{"Key":"complaints","Title":"Protests","Items":["Only a Studio Director or Teacher may start a protest.","Levels may not be protested, because they are an opinion.","Protests must be signed and given in writing to the director of the show within 30 minutes of the incident. Protests are not accepted after an awards ceremony."]},{"Key":"other","Title":"National Championships Extras","Items":["Free Master Classes: 2 to 3 classes taught by industry professionals, on stage, listed in the Nationals Overview.","Free Opening Number taught by a legendary choreographer, for Grand Prix performers and select Accelerating Stars performers aged 12 and over. Dancers must have group routines attending Nationals. Each studio nominates performers.","Driven Moves, the Parent Improv Challenge: a free, parents-only improv competition. Space is limited and registration is at the Registration Desk only.","Single age divisions (4 to 19) are printed for Jazz, Tap, Lyrical, Contemporary and Open. The template carries the six standard age divisions."]}],"Documents":[{"Title":"2026 Official Rules & Regulations","Url":"https://driventalentcompetition.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/2026-Driven-Talent-Competition-4.pdf"}]}`),t=[{ParticipantType:"Individual",Source:"2026 Official Rules & Regulations, General Divisions",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["A soloist may not compete against themselves in the same performance category.","Starting Line and Breaking Boundaries soloists may enter at most 2 solos. Other soloists may enter at most 3 solo performance categories (Vocal solos are not counted).","A soloist may not place more than once in the High Score Division.","Time limit for a solo is 2:45."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- A soloist may not compete against themselves in the same performance category.
- Starting Line and Breaking Boundaries soloists may enter at most 2 solos. Other soloists may enter at most 3 solo performance categories (Vocal solos are not counted).
- A soloist may not place more than once in the High Score Division.
- Time limit for a solo is 2:45.`},{ParticipantType:"Team",Source:"2026 Official Rules & Regulations, General Divisions and Levels",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["Duet/Trio 2 to 3 performers (2:45); Small Group 4 to 9 (3:00); Large Group 10 to 19 (4:00); Line 20 or more (4:30).","Groups perform with the number of performers they registered. A missing or added performer may move the routine to another size, or to adjudication only.","The routine takes the average age of its dancers, decimals dropped.","Small Groups and Duet/Trios take the highest level of any performer. Large Groups and Lines may have at most one third of performers in a higher level."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- Duet/Trio 2 to 3 performers (2:45); Small Group 4 to 9 (3:00); Large Group 10 to 19 (4:00); Line 20 or more (4:30).
- Groups perform with the number of performers they registered. A missing or added performer may move the routine to another size, or to adjudication only.
- The routine takes the average age of its dancers, decimals dropped.
- Small Groups and Duet/Trios take the highest level of any performer. Large Groups and Lines may have at most one third of performers in a higher level.`}],i=[],a=JSON.parse('[{"Title":"Acro/Gymnastics","Source":"2026 Official Rules & Regulations, Performance Divisions","Sections":{"About":["A routine that contains mainly gymnastic tricks such as walkovers, front or back limbers, handstands, headstands and cartwheels, with a blend of gymnastics and dance."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":null,"Allowed":["No limit on acro and gymnastic tricks."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- A routine that contains mainly gymnastic tricks such as walkovers, front or back limbers, handstands, headstands and cartwheels, with a blend of gymnastics and dance.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- No limit on acro and gymnastic tricks."},{"Title":"Ballet","Source":"2026 Official Rules & Regulations, Performance Divisions","Sections":{"About":["Classical steps and formal ballet technique."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Ballet shoes must be worn."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["No pointe shoes.","No acro or gymnastics tricks."],"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Classical steps and formal ballet technique.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Ballet shoes must be worn.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- No pointe shoes.\\n- No acro or gymnastics tricks."},{"Title":"Ballroom","Source":"2026 Official Rules & Regulations, Performance Divisions","Sections":{"About":["Standard or Latin Ballroom technique."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Performed with ballroom heels or ballroom shoes only."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Standard or Latin Ballroom technique.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Performed with ballroom heels or ballroom shoes only."},{"Title":"Baton","Source":"2026 Official Rules & Regulations, Performance Divisions","Sections":{"About":["A routine using baton(s) and baton technique."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":null,"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Judged on baton technique, dance technique and choreography."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- A routine using baton(s) and baton technique.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judged on baton technique, dance technique and choreography."},{"Title":"Character","Source":"2026 Official Rules & Regulations, Performance Divisions","Sections":{"About":["A routine that portrays a character easily recognized from a movie, music video, pop culture or history."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":null,"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- A routine that portrays a character easily recognized from a movie, music video, pop culture or history."},{"Title":"Cheerleading","Source":"2026 Official Rules & Regulations, Performance Divisions","Sections":{"About":["Cheerleading technique with strong, sharp movements, vocal cheering and dance."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":null,"Allowed":["May contain up to 50 percent acro/gymnastics."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Cheerleading technique with strong, sharp movements, vocal cheering and dance.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- May contain up to 50 percent acro/gymnastics."},{"Title":"Clogging","Source":"2026 Official Rules & Regulations, Performance Divisions","Sections":{"About":["A routine using clogging technique."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Performers wear clogging shoes."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- A routine using clogging technique.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Performers wear clogging shoes."},{"Title":"Contemporary","Source":"2026 Official Rules & Regulations, Performance Divisions","Sections":{"About":["Combines ballet technique, lyrical and modern movements in a unique way."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":null,"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":["The rules print single age divisions (4 to 19) for this category."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Combines ballet technique, lyrical and modern movements in a unique way.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- The rules print single age divisions (4 to 19) for this category."},{"Title":"Folkloric","Source":"2026 Official Rules & Regulations, Performance Divisions","Sections":{"About":["Ethnic styles of dance and technique, such as traditional Asian dances, Hawaiian and Spanish Flamenco."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":null,"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Ethnic styles of dance and technique, such as traditional Asian dances, Hawaiian and Spanish Flamenco."},{"Title":"Hip Hop","Source":"2026 Official Rules & Regulations, Performance Divisions","Sections":{"About":["The latest street dance style, as seen in current pop culture and artist tours and performances."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":null,"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- The latest street dance style, as seen in current pop culture and artist tours and performances."},{"Title":"Jazz","Source":"2026 Official Rules & Regulations, Performance Divisions","Sections":{"About":["Traditional jazz technique such as pirouettes, isolations and leaps."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":null,"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":["The rules print single age divisions (4 to 19) for this category."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Traditional jazz technique such as pirouettes, isolations and leaps.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- The rules print single age divisions (4 to 19) for this category."},{"Title":"Lyrical","Source":"2026 Official Rules & Regulations, Performance Divisions","Sections":{"About":["A routine performed to the lyrics or mood of the music, with balance, extension and control to slower rhythms."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":null,"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":["The rules print single age divisions (4 to 19) for this category."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- A routine performed to the lyrics or mood of the music, with balance, extension and control to slower rhythms.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- The rules print single age divisions (4 to 19) for this category."},{"Title":"Modern","Source":"2026 Official Rules & Regulations, Performance Divisions","Sections":{"About":["An interpretive style using modern techniques such as Graham, Ailey and Horton."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":null,"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- An interpretive style using modern techniques such as Graham, Ailey and Horton."},{"Title":"Musical Theater","Source":"2026 Official Rules & Regulations, Performance Divisions","Sections":{"About":["A routine to the music of a Broadway or movie musical, or with characters from a known Broadway or movie musical."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":null,"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- A routine to the music of a Broadway or movie musical, or with characters from a known Broadway or movie musical."},{"Title":"Open","Source":"2026 Official Rules & Regulations, Performance Divisions","Sections":{"About":["A routine that does not fit one category, or combines any of the other categories."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":null,"Allowed":["No limit on acro and gymnastic tricks."],"NotAllowed":["No pointe.","No vocals."],"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":["The rules print single age divisions (4 to 19) for this category."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- A routine that does not fit one category, or combines any of the other categories.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- No limit on acro and gymnastic tricks.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- No pointe.\\n- No vocals.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- The rules print single age divisions (4 to 19) for this category."},{"Title":"Pointe","Source":"2026 Official Rules & Regulations, Performance Divisions","Sections":{"About":["Ballet, pointe and toe technique."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Grand Prix and Accelerating Stars levels only.","Pointe shoes must be worn."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Ballet, pointe and toe technique.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Grand Prix and Accelerating Stars levels only.\\n- Pointe shoes must be worn."},{"Title":"Pom Pon","Source":"2026 Official Rules & Regulations, Performance Divisions","Sections":{"About":["Dance with pom pons used for at least 75 percent of the routine."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":null,"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Formations and staging are highly considered."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Dance with pom pons used for at least 75 percent of the routine.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Formations and staging are highly considered."},{"Title":"Song and Dance","Source":"2026 Official Rules & Regulations, Performance Divisions","Sections":{"About":["Any listed dance category combined with singing. Both singing and dancing must be present and are judged."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Two handheld wireless microphones are provided."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Lead vocals may not be lip synced; only backup vocal accompaniment may be recorded.","No personal or studio microphones or headsets."],"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Any listed dance category combined with singing. Both singing and dancing must be present and are judged.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Two handheld wireless microphones are provided.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Lead vocals may not be lip synced; only backup vocal accompaniment may be recorded.\\n- No personal or studio microphones or headsets."},{"Title":"Tap","Source":"2026 Official Rules & Regulations, Performance Divisions","Sections":{"About":["A routine using rhythm and tap technique."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Performed with tap shoes only."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["No recorded tap sounds in the music."],"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":["The rules print single age divisions (4 to 19) for this category."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- A routine using rhythm and tap technique.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Performed with tap shoes only.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- No recorded tap sounds in the music.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- The rules print single age divisions (4 to 19) for this category."},{"Title":"Vocal","Source":"2026 Official Rules & Regulations, Performance Divisions","Sections":{"About":["Any type of vocal-only performance."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Accompaniment must be pre-recorded.","Two handheld wireless microphones are provided.","All Vocals default to the Grand Prix level."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["No recorded lead vocals.","No personal or studio microphones or headsets in the sound system."],"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":["Vocal solos are not counted in the solo entry limit."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Any type of vocal-only performance.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Accompaniment must be pre-recorded.\\n- Two handheld wireless microphones are provided.\\n- All Vocals default to the Grand Prix level.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- No recorded lead vocals.\\n- No personal or studio microphones or headsets in the sound system.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Vocal solos are not counted in the solo entry limit."},{"Title":"Production Line","Source":"2026 Official Rules & Regulations, General Divisions and Levels","Sections":{"About":["20 or more performers. No specific category (Jazz, Tap, Lyrical and so on) and no level choice."],"TimeAndFormat":["Time limit 7:00. Extended time is available in 1 minute steps: {{ExtendedTimeFee}}."],"Rules":["All Production Lines are placed in the Grand Prix level."],"Allowed":["No limit on acro and gymnastic tricks.","A Senior performer may join a younger routine."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["High Score age divisions are 11 and Under and 12 and Over."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- 20 or more performers. No specific category (Jazz, Tap, Lyrical and so on) and no level choice.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Time limit 7:00. Extended time is available in 1 minute steps: {{ExtendedTimeFee}}.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- All Production Lines are placed in the Grand Prix level.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- No limit on acro and gymnastic tricks.\\n- A Senior performer may join a younger routine.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- High Score age divisions are 11 and Under and 12 and Over."},{"Title":"Miss and Mr Driven Title","Source":"2026 Official Rules & Regulations, Title Competition","Sections":{"About":["Added to the solo division at every regional event. Open to Accelerating Stars and Grand Prix soloists."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Tick the Title box when registering the solo, or register at the door at least 1 hour before the performance.","A performer may enter at most 3 solos for Title.","A regional Title Champion may not repeat the same routine for Title at another regional, but may use a different routine."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Judged on showmanship, style and overall presentation during the solo.","Maximum 10 points from each judge."],"Points":["Awards go to the male and female Title Champions and the 1st and 2nd runners-up in each age division.","Title age divisions: 5 and under, 6 to 8, 9 to 11, 12 to 14, 15 to 19."],"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Added to the solo division at every regional event. Open to Accelerating Stars and Grand Prix soloists.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Tick the Title box when registering the solo, or register at the door at least 1 hour before the performance.\\n- A performer may enter at most 3 solos for Title.\\n- A regional Title Champion may not repeat the same routine for Title at another regional, but may use a different routine.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judged on showmanship, style and overall presentation during the solo.\\n- Maximum 10 points from each judge.\\n\\n## Points\\n- Awards go to the male and female Title Champions and the 1st and 2nd runners-up in each age division.\\n- Title age divisions: 5 and under, 6 to 8, 9 to 11, 12 to 14, 15 to 19."},{"Title":"Driven Cypher Improv","Source":"2026 Official Rules & Regulations, Additional Events at National Championships","Sections":{"About":["An optional improv competition at National Championships with two divisions: 11 and Under and 12 and Over."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Entry is {{CypherFee}}, registered at the Registration Desk.","Space is limited.","More details are shared closer to Nationals."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- An optional improv competition at National Championships with two divisions: 11 and Under and 12 and Over.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Entry is {{CypherFee}}, registered at the Registration Desk.\\n- Space is limited.\\n- More details are shared closer to Nationals."}]'),r=[],s=[{Key:"AgeCutoffDate",Kind:"date",Label:"Date on which ages are calculated",Value:"2025-12-31",Source:"2026 Official Rules & Regulations, Age Divisions (age as of December 31st, 2025)"},{Key:"PaymentLevel1",Kind:"text",Label:"Price level 1",Value:"Paid in full 60 or more days before the event",Source:"2026 Official Rules & Regulations, Payments"},{Key:"PaymentLevel2",Kind:"text",Label:"Price level 2",Value:"Paid in full 31 to 59 days before the event",Source:"2026 Official Rules & Regulations, Payments"},{Key:"PaymentLevel3",Kind:"text",Label:"Price level 3",Value:"Paid in full 30 days before the event",Source:"2026 Official Rules & Regulations, Payments"},{Key:"ChangeFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Late change fee",Value:"USD 10 per change, for changes made less than 21 days before the event",Source:"2026 Official Rules & Regulations, Payments"},{Key:"ExtendedTimeFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Extended time for groups and lines",Value:"USD 4 per performer for each 30 second step (USD 4 per performer for each 1 minute step for Production Lines)",Source:"2026 Official Rules & Regulations, Extended Times"},{Key:"PropTimeFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Extended prop time",Value:"USD 25 for up to 3 minutes; USD 50 for anything over 4 minutes",Source:"2026 Official Rules & Regulations, Props"},{Key:"CostumeContestFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Costume contest entry",Value:"A fee is charged (the amount is not printed in the rules)",Source:"2026 Official Rules & Regulations, Costume Award"},{Key:"CypherFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Driven Cypher improv entry (Nationals)",Value:"USD 35",Source:"2026 Official Rules & Regulations, Additional events at National Championships"},{Key:"DrivenDollarsSolo",Kind:"prize",Label:"Driven Dollars for a Grand Prix solo (1st overall)",Value:"USD 100 (1-350 entries), USD 150 (351-500), USD 200 (501 and up)",Source:"2026 Official Rules & Regulations, Adjudication of Awards"},{Key:"DrivenDollarsDuetTrio",Kind:"prize",Label:"Driven Dollars for a Grand Prix duet/trio",Value:"USD 150 (1-350 entries), USD 200 (351-500), USD 250 (501 and up)",Source:"2026 Official Rules & Regulations, Adjudication of Awards"},{Key:"DrivenDollarsGroup",Kind:"prize",Label:"Driven Dollars for a Grand Prix small or large group",Value:"USD 200 (1-350 entries), USD 250 (351-500), USD 300 (501 and up)",Source:"2026 Official Rules & Regulations, Adjudication of Awards"},{Key:"DrivenDollarsLine",Kind:"prize",Label:"Driven Dollars for a Grand Prix line or production line",Value:"USD 250 (1-350 entries), USD 300 (351-500), USD 350 (501 and up)",Source:"2026 Official Rules & Regulations, Adjudication of Awards"},{Key:"IndustryIconDollars",Kind:"prize",Label:"Industry Icon Award Driven Dollars",Value:"USD 300 (1-350 entries), USD 400 (351-500), USD 500 (501 and up)",Source:"2026 Official Rules & Regulations, Additional Awards"},{Key:"RulesDocumentLink",Kind:"link",Label:"Official rules PDF",Value:"https://driventalentcompetition.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/2026-Driven-Talent-Competition-4.pdf",Source:"Organiser website"}],l=[{Claim:"Rules, levels, awards and fees as printed in the organiser's 2026 Official Rules & Regulations.",SourceType:"Primary - the event's own rules document",Source:"2026 Official Rules & Regulations",Url:"https://driventalentcompetition.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/2026-Driven-Talent-Competition-4.pdf"}],u={TemplateKey:e,Year:2026,Note:o,Page:n,ParticipantTypes:t,AgeGroups:i,Competitions:a,CompetitionAgeGroups:r,Variables:s,Evidence:l};export{i as AgeGroups,r as CompetitionAgeGroups,a as Competitions,l as Evidence,o as Note,n as Page,t as ParticipantTypes,e as TemplateKey,s as Variables,d as Year,u as default};
